43
00:02:54.983 --> 00:02:58.353
Clean energy cooperation lowered the cost of batteries.

44
00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:02.554
Your turn. Say: Clean energy cooperation.

45
00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:07.667
Clean energy cooperation.

46
00:03:08.467 --> 00:03:11.967
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:03:12.817 --> 00:03:20.879
Visal, an analyst writes 'Owing to the crisis, prices rose, thereby increasing pressure on governments.' What do 'owing to' and 'thereby' do?

48
00:03:21.983 --> 00:03:36.269
'Owing to' and 'as a result of' are followed by a noun and show the cause. 'Thereby' + -ing shows the result of the action before it, with the same subject: prices rose, thereby increasing pressure.

49
00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:38.884
Can I use 'because' there?

50
00:03:39.983 --> 00:03:50.069
'Because' needs a clause: 'because the crisis began'. 'Because of', 'due to' and 'owing to' need a noun phrase. Choose by what follows.

51
00:03:51.183 --> 00:03:52.440
What about 'thus'?

52
00:03:53.550 --> 00:04:04.225
'Thus' and 'hence' are formal linkers for results: 'Supplies fell; thus, prices rose.' Put a semicolon or full stop before thus and a comma after it.

53
00:04:05.367 --> 00:04:06.890
Part three: grammar.

54
00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:13.151
Grammar focus: Cause and result: owing to and thereby plus -ing and thus.

55
00:04:13.451 --> 00:04:14.650
Look at the pattern.

56
00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:20.867
Owing to the energy crisis, prices rose sharply, thereby increasing pressure on governments.

57
00:04:21.783 --> 00:04:26.848
As a result of pipeline politics, supplies were cut, and several cities lost heat.

58
00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:31.503
Exporters raised output; thus, prices fell the following year.

59
00:04:32.467 --> 00:04:41.014
Use owing to / due to / as a result of + noun for causes, thereby + -ing for a result with the same subject, and thus / hence + comma as formal linkers.

60
00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:45.250
Be careful! Don't say: Owing to it rained, we stayed.

61
00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:49.594
Say: Owing to the rain, we stayed.

62
00:04:49.894 --> 00:04:52.149
After 'owing to', use a noun phrase.

63
00:04:52.933 --> 00:04:55.737
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:56.533 --> 00:04:58.626
Power, Pipelines and Politics.

65
00:04:58.926 --> 00:05:04.687
Energy security means having reliable and affordable power, and oil dependency can weaken it.

66
00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:11.937
Owing to pipeline politics, some countries have cut supplies, thereby gaining leverage over their customers.

67
00:05:12.933 --> 00:05:19.937
An energy exporter earns enormous income, and a strategic reserve gives importers time to react during an energy crisis.

68
00:05:20.933 --> 00:05:27.670
As a result of the renewable energy transition, new partnerships are emerging, thus changing old alliances.

69
00:05:28.667 --> 00:05:34.010
Clean energy cooperation spreads technology and lowers costs for everyone.

70
00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:39.171
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:05:40.017 --> 00:05:42.504
blank the storm, the pipeline was closed.

72
00:05:42.804 --> 00:05:46.179
A, Because. B, Owing to. C, Although.

73
00:05:49.733 --> 00:05:51.524
The answer is B: Owing to.

74
00:05:52.683 --> 00:05:55.635
Which linker needs a noun phrase, not a clause?

75
00:05:55.935 --> 00:05:59.565
A, because of. B, because. C, although.

76
00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:05.169
The answer is A: because of.

77
00:06:06.317 --> 00:06:08.049
Choose the correct sentence.

78
00:06:08.349 --> 00:06:17.157
A, Prices rose, thereby increase pressure.. B, Prices rose, thereby increasing pressure.. C, Prices rose, thereby increased pressure..

79
00:06:20.700 --> 00:06:24.499
The answer is B: Prices rose, thereby increasing pressure..

80
00:06:25.650 --> 00:06:30.285
A stock of oil that a government keeps for emergencies is a strategic blank.

81
00:06:30.585 --> 00:06:34.029
A, reserve. B, treaty. C, debris.

82
00:06:37.567 --> 00:06:39.357
The answer is A: reserve.

83
00:06:40.517 --> 00:06:44.676
According to the reading, what does a strategic reserve give importers?

84
00:06:44.976 --> 00:06:49.628
A, time to react. B, extra tariffs. C, new borders.

85
00:06:53.167 --> 00:06:55.247
The answer is A: time to react.

86
00:06:56.433 --> 00:06:59.759
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:07:00.617 --> 00:07:04.648
How might a shift to renewable energy change global energy diplomacy?

88
00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:14.915
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:07:15.215 --> 00:07:45.758
A shift to renewable energy could reduce the power of oil and gas exporters, because every country can generate some electricity from sun and wind. Energy security would depend more on technology, minerals and electricity networks than on pipeline politics. New partnerships may appear around clean energy cooperation, but countries rich in critical minerals could gain influence.

90
00:07:46.058 --> 00:07:47.929
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:48.817 --> 00:07:55.602
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and cause and result: owing to and thereby plus -ing and thus.

92
00:07:55.902 --> 00:08:00.969
Today's value is strategic thinking. Think ahead, and choose your path with purpose.

93
00:08:01.269 --> 00:08:04.200
See you in Unit seventeen. Goodbye!

94
00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:07.489
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

